  "name": "Torres Strait island style (Thursday Island string-band song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Secular popular song of Thursday Island and the Torres Strait that grew out of the pearling era, when Islander, Malay, Filipino, Japanese and Pacific Islander crews shared sea songs, Hawaiian and Pacific string-band tunes, blues and popular ballads; it is sung to acoustic guitar and ukulele at parties and social gatherings. The former pearl diver Seaman Dan (Henry Gibson Dan) recorded the style late in life, and his albums won ARIA awards for world music.",
